-- SQL script to update existing hackathons with full descriptions
UPDATE public.events SET description = 'About the Hackathon: The Stellan AI Buildathon 2026 is a national-level online hackathon designed for students, developers, innovators, and aspiring entrepreneurs who want to build the next generation of AI-powered products. Participants will have the opportunity to solve real-world challenges using Artificial Intelligence, Automation, No-Code Tools, AI Agents, and Emerging Technologies while competing for scholarships, mentorship, internships, and exclusive opportunities. Whether you''re a beginner exploring AI or an experienced builder creating innovative solutions, this hackathon provides the perfect platform to learn, build, and showcase your skills. Theme: Build the Future with AI Create solutions that leverage AI to solve problems in: Education Healthcare Business &amp; Productivity Finance Sustainability Smart Cities Agriculture Creator Economy Student Life Social Impact Eligibility: Undergraduate Students Postgraduate Students Recent Graduates Individual Participants Teams of up to 4 Members Participants from all academic disciplines are welcome. Hackathon Format: Round 1: Idea Submission Submit: Problem Statement Proposed Solution AI Implementation Approach Round 2: Prototype Development Shortlisted teams will develop: MVP AI Solution Automation Workflow AI Agent Web Application Mobile Application Round 3: Final Presentation Present your solution to a panel of mentors, founders, and industry experts. Judging Criteria: Innovation &amp; Creativity Problem-Solving Ability AI Integration Technical Implementation Business Potential User Experience Presentation Quality Rewards &amp; Benefits: Winner 100% Scholarship for the Stellan AI Builder Diploma Program Guaranteed Interview for Internship Opportunities Founder Mentorship Certificate of Excellence First Runner-Up 80% Scholarship for the Stellan AI Builder Diploma Program Career Mentorship Internship Opportunities Second Runner-Up 60% Scholarship for the Stellan AI Builder Diploma Program Industry Mentorship Top 20 Teams Exclusive Builder Community Access Networking Opportunities Special Recognition Certificates All Participants Participation Certificate Access to Exclusive AI Learning Resources Community Membership Why Participate?: Build Real-World AI Projects Showcase Your Skills Gain Industry Exposure Win Scholarships Worth Lakhs Connect with Founders and Mentors Access Internship Opportunities Join a Community of Builders and Innovators' WHERE link = 'https://unstop.com/hackathons/stellan-ai-buildathon-2026-dyndox-1697660';
UPDATE public.events SET description = 'About the Opportunity: With the successful conclusion of MSME Launchpad 2.0, Prodmark Business Consultants Private Limited now presents Tech Launchpad 1.0, an exciting online coding challenge designed for teams to showcase their technical prowess. This event provides a dynamic platform for participants to collaborate and develop innovative solutions in a virtual environment. Problem: Our one of the offerings through MBA Partner (www.mbapartner.in) requires a dynamic website and an application that includes all the possible content that an MBA student requires including, but not limited to, Live Projects, Placements Prep, Case Competitions, Repositories, and Past year testimonials. While we have all these in the best of our capabilities with amazing set of Old IIM Mentors producing magnificent results for 2000+ students in the past, our website doesn''t show it in the best possible manner. Solution: We need a website and a mobile application with amazing UI/UX and an AI Chatbot that helps students navigate through the offerings and get a best experience even before enrollment. Our current website is hosted on Wix and hence, our preference would be to have an alternative one built on the same and integrate it with our existing one. If website built on external platforms can be integrated into Wix, that works as well Eligibility and Registration: This opportunity is open to Team Participation of maximum 3. Seize this chance to join the Tech Launchpad 1.0 online coding challenge and make your mark! Certificates of Appreciation would be given to each one of you.' WHERE link = 'https://unstop.com/hackathons/tech-launchpad-10-prodmark-business-consultants-private-limited-1696924';
UPDATE public.events SET description = '76% of India''s 1.5 million clinics still run on paper token slips and shouting. Patients wait 2&ndash;3 hours with zero visibility into when they''ll be called. Doctors have no dashboard. Receptionists manage everything from memory. You''re going to fix that. Queue Cure ''26 is a beginner-friendly Full Stack hackathon hosted on Wooble &mdash; India''s portfolio-first hiring platform where builders get hired on what they build, not what their resume says. What to build: Screen 1 &mdash; Receptionist view: Add patient, call next token, set average consultation time Screen 2 &mdash; Patient waiting room view: Current token being seen, tokens ahead, estimated wait Live sync &mdash; both screens update the moment "Call Next" is clicked Submission Requirements Submit all 4 of the following to your Wooble portfolio: Working prototype link or demo video GitHub repository with README Socket event diagram Thought process sheet Evaluation Criteria Criteria Weight Live queue updates correctly across both screens without refresh 40% Wait time computed from real data &mdash; not hardcoded 25% Receptionist screen is fast and mistake-proof 20% Thought process addresses concurrency and edge cases 15% Participant Benefits Participation Certificate Winner Certificate + LinkedIn Badge Portfolio feature on Wooble Interview Opportunity with hiring partners Talent Pool Shortlisting for future roles' WHERE link = 'https://unstop.com/hackathons/queue-cure-26-wooble-software-private-limited-1697413';
UPDATE public.events SET description = 'Ship to Get Hired &mdash; Gappy AI Hackathon Build a real AI product. Get hired. Win ₹1 Lakh. At a Glance Registration: Rolling &mdash; June 8&ndash;29 Build window: June 24&ndash;30 Who can build: Developers, PMs, operators &amp; students Career: Hiring fast-track to partner companies Proof: Project certificates Not just for developers. With Lemma SDK you can build entirely through prompting &mdash; no deep coding background needed. What matters most is clear thinking: a sharply defined problem, real product sense, and the judgment to ship something people would actually use. Developers, PMs, operators, and students are all welcome. What You''ll Build: Build a working agentic app using Lemma SDK as your infrastructure layer. Lemma SDK is upcoming (launching on 24th June) open-source infrastructure for coding agents to build agentic apps that run real work. It provisions ai agents, datastores, document stores, frontend, backend, workflows, functions, and integrations to build ai apps end to end. Pick any real-world problem: a specific user, a clear pain point, and a workflow worth solving. Or build from one of our curated problem statements (to be shared over email after registration) The core loop should work end-to-end and be demoable. Bring your own IDE, AI coding tool, API key, builder platform, and hosting/deployment setup. The Hiring Fast-Track Your submission goes to work for you: Submissions are evaluated for problem clarity, product thinking, and execution quality. Top builders are matched to AI Product Engineer and AI Product Manager roles (full-time and internship role) at partner companies. Your profile &mdash; resume, project summary, and a written rationale &mdash; goes directly to the hiring team. No cold applications. Partner companies may invite you directly for a first-round interview. No CV screening, no recruiter filters. Hiring partners: YesMadam &middot; Binocs &middot; Foxo &middot; Zapdata &middot; Corally The Project Track (for top 10 teams, optional): Top 10 teams get the chance to keep building &mdash; with the Lemma team behind them: Two more weeks to refine your submission into a full-fledged product, with direct guidance on architecture, SDK usage, and product decisions. A verified project certificate of contribution &mdash; a real credential, not participation filler. The strongest projects published on the Lemma website as community templates. Timeline: June 8&ndash;29 &mdash; Rolling registrations (the hackathon begins June 24) June 24 &mdash; Lemma SDK launches publicly + build window begins June 30 &mdash; Submissions close (project + short writeup + working demo) After judging &mdash; Results announced. Winners recognised, and shortlisted builders'' profiles matched and introduced to partner companies. Partner companies may invite you directly for a first-round interview. How We Judge Problem clarity &amp; real-world fit &mdash; 35% Product judgment &mdash; 25% Execution quality &mdash; 25% Lemma SDK utilisation &mdash; 15% What is Lemma? Most software records what happened. Lemma is infrastructure for software that actually does the work &mdash; structured data, AI agents, automated workflows, and custom interfaces in one environment. The SDK is open-source and locally runnable, and it launches publicly on June 24 &mdash; the same day the hackathon begins, so everyone starts fresh.' WHERE link = 'https://unstop.com/hackathons/gappy-ai-hackathon-gappy-ai-1694233';
UPDATE public.events SET description = 'HACKDAY.EXE 2.0 is a 10-hour non-stop virtual hackathon where developers, designers, and problem solvers come together to build AI-powered applications and ship real projects within a single day. join now&nbsp; https://discord.gg/zn4DeAq8d Platform The hackathon will be conducted entirely online via Discord. All announcements, team formation, opening ceremony, mentorship sessions, and event updates will take place on Discord. Participants must join the Discord server before the event begins. Format 10-hour virtual hackathon Individual participation only Opening ceremony on Discord Final submissions through Unstop Prize Categories 1. Best Use of AI APIs Build innovative solutions using Gemini API, Google Cloud AI, or other cutting-edge AI APIs and developer tools. 2. Best Deployed App Develop and deploy a live, production-ready application on cloud infrastructure. Rewards Winners (1st and 2nd place) in each category will receive exclusive gadgets, goodies, official stickers, and sponsor merchandise. Participation certificates will be provided to all participants. Eligibility Open to students, freshers, and developers. No prior experience required. Participants from any college, university, or professional background can apply. Rules &amp; Guidelines Projects must be built entirely during the hackathon window. Gemini API, Google Cloud, or another AI API must be used as a core component of the project. Each participant can submit only one project. Plagiarism or pre-built projects will result in immediate disqualification. All participants must be registered on Unstop. Hackathon Process Step 1 Register on Unstop. Step 2 Join the official Discord server. Step 3 Attend the opening ceremony on 13 June 2026 at 12:00 PM UTC . Step 4 Build your project using Gemini API, Google Cloud, or any AI API. Step 5 Submit your project via Unstop before 10:00 PM UTC . Recommended Tools &amp; APIs Gemini API (Google AI Studio) Google Cloud Platform (GCP) Claude API Other AI and cloud-based APIs' WHERE link = 'https://unstop.com/hackathons/hackdayexe-20-vel-tech-rangarajan-dr-sagunthala-r-d-institute-of-science-and-technology-1696682';
UPDATE public.events SET description = '​Every single day, dozens of conventional hackathons take place across the country. ​Thousands of developers write rushed, unstructured code over a weekend, claim prizes, pack up, and abandon their repositories forever. ​This is the Mirage. ​High-value cloud resources are burned, sponsor APIs are temporarily activated, and developer retention drops to absolute zero. ​The Black-Box Protocol is explicitly engineered to smash this cycle. ​We are introducing an interconnected, campaign-driven technical universe where products don''t die&mdash;they undergo structural incubation. Just like a cinematic universe, your progress in Stage 01 carries directly into subsequent stages, culminating in the Singularity Protocol (Stage 05) and final market scaling. Welcome to Stage 01 // "System Escalation "&mdash;the genesis node focusing on the absolute convergence of autonomous AI agents and decentralized Web3 ledger technology. The 2-Round Hybrid Architecture &amp; Execution Model ​To ensure an uncompromised signal-to-noise ratio, we are implementing a strict, multi-stage gatekeeper pipeline. To survive the protocol and reach the Gwalior finale, your team must clear both phases. Round 01 // Registration &amp; System Architecture Screening ​ (Online) ​Timeline: ​June 04 &ndash; June 15, 2026 ​Key Windows: Registration Window: ​June 05 &ndash; June 13, 2026 ​System Blueprint Submission (PPT/Abstract): ​June 10 &ndash; June 15, 2026 Protocol Challenge (60 Minutes): ​June 15, 2026 ​Results Declaration &amp; Access Codes Release: ​June 19 or June 20, 2026 ​ Round 01 Execution Model (step-By-Step) ​ The Portal Onboarding (June 04 - June 13) ​Register your team (2 to 4 developers) on Luma. Provide active GitHub profiles and select your core technical domains (AI orchestration, smart contracts, or UI/system architecture). ​ The Blueprint Blueprinting (June 10 - June 15) ​Shortlisted teams will gain access to the submission portal. You must submit a 6-slide System Architecture Blueprint (PPT/PDF) detailing: ​Problem Statement &amp; Proposed Use Case ​Technical Architecture Diagram mapping the precise data flow between your ​Autonomous AI Agent and the Layer-1 blockchain ​Proposed Sponsor Tool Integration and API/SDK deployment logic The Protocol Challenge (June 15) ​All participants must complete a mandatory 60-minute online challenge designed to evaluate technical knowledge, practical problem-solving ability, and domain expertise in ​building production-grade AI systems. ​The challenge will be based on the official Stage 01 tracks: On&nbsp;HiDevs Platform ​ Gen AI Products: ​Reliability &amp; Monitoring ​Cost &amp; Latency Optimization ​Participants can expect a mix of: ​System Design Questions ​Scenario-Based Problem Solving ​Architecture Analysis ​GenAI Infrastructure Concepts ​Production Deployment Challenges ​The objective is to evaluate a participant''s ability to design, optimize, monitor, and scale real-world GenAI applications beyond simple prototypes. ​Challenge scores will be reflected on the official leaderboard and will contribute directly to the Round 01 evaluation process. ​ The Core Filter (June 16 - June 18) ​Our industry mentors will audit every blueprint submission and challenge result. ​We evaluate: ​Originality ​Logic Validity ​Technical Depth ​System Design Quality ​Execution Potential ​Plagiarized projects, low-intent AI wrappers, or technically invalid architectures will be ​eliminated immediately. ​ Access Codes Release (June 19 / June 20) ​Only the top 50&ndash;60 teams will receive physical terminal clearance codes to enter Gwalior. ​Round 02 qualification is determined through the following: ​System Architecture Blueprint Submission ​Technical Challenge Leaderboard Performance ​Teams must demonstrate both strong architectural thinking and technical competency to advance. Round 02 // the Terminal Lockdown (8-Hour Offline Finale) ​Timeline: ​4th Week of June 2026 ​Location: ​Gwalior, Madhya Pradesh ​(with hybrid channels for global remote tracks) ​Format: ​A strict, non-stop 8/12-hour continuous offline hacking sprint. ​ Round 02 Execution Model (step-By-Step) ​ Deployment &amp; Gating (Hour 00) ​Selected teams arrive at the Gwalior physical hub. ​Outstation participants gain access to designated storage and preparation areas for ​their equipment and belongings. ​ The Network Ignition (Hour 01) ​Teams connect to the central coding arena. Each team receives dedicated power access and uninterrupted high-speed connectivity. ​ The Terminal Lockdown (Hours 01 - 08) ​A continuous, high-pressure hacking window. ​Teams must live-code, test, and deploy their MVPs. ​No Slide Preparation Allowed. ​Teams must focus entirely on building, testing, and deployment. ​Mandatory Stack Integration: ​Projects must actively execute sponsor APIs, AI workflows, cloud infrastructure, or blockchain smart contracts. ​ The System Recharge (Hour 04) ​Dedicated lunch, snacks, beverages, and hydration stations will remain available throughout the event. ​ The Submission Protocol (Final Hour) ​All teams must submit their final projects through the HiDevs Platform . ​Submission Requirements: ​GitHub Repository ​Live Demo Link ​Technical Documentation ​Project Overview ​Sponsor Integration Details ​ The Live-Execution Jury (Hour 08+) ​No dry pitching. ​Evaluation is based strictly on live execution. ​Teams must demonstrate: ​Functional MVP ​Autonomous AI Agent Workflows ​Smart Contract Execution ​API Transaction Logs ​Deployment Status ​GitHub Commit History The Value Matrix (what Is in The Box?) ​ Incentive Pool: ​Up to 50K+ in developer bounty pools, cash prizes, sponsor rewards, and hardware incentives. ​ Continuous Incubation: ​Access to a 6&ndash;12 month post-event support pipeline connecting projects with mentors, accelerators, investors, and ecosystem partners. ​ Expert Mentorship: ​Real-time architecture reviews, technical guidance, and execution-focused feedback from industry specialists. ​ Registration Compliance Rules ​ Repository Integrity: ​All code must be initialized and systematically committed during active round windows. ​Pre-existing, copy-pasted, or white-labeled projects trigger immediate disqualification. ​ Mandatory Convergence: ​Projects must functionalize both domains. ​An AI wrapper without Web3 trust, or a Web3 contract without autonomous AI capabilities, will not pass Round 01. Strict Gatekeeping: Registrations &nbsp;are limited and subject to manual review. ​Ensure all submitted information is accurate. For More Updates:&nbsp; Join WhatsApp Group' WHERE link = 'https://unstop.com/hackathons/the-black-box-protocol-stage-01-system-escalation-samrat-ashok-technological-institute-sati-vidisha-1695117';
UPDATE public.events SET description = 'About the Competition WebForge is a project-based web development competition organized by IEEE Computational Intelligence Society (CIS), MUJ. The event is designed to challenge participants to develop innovative web-based solutions that address real-world problems through technology, creativity, and effective design. Participants will showcase their skills in web development, UI/UX design, problem-solving, teamwork, and project presentation while competing against talented developers from diverse backgrounds. The competition encourages innovation, technical excellence, and user-centric thinking, providing a platform for participants to transform ideas into impactful digital solutions. Eligibility Open to all students. Participants may register individually or as a team. Inter-college teams are allowed. Inter-branch teams are allowed. Participants must complete registration through Unstop before the deadline. Team Rules Each team can have 1 to 3 members . Teams can use any tech stack such as HTML, CSS, JavaScript, React, Node.js, MongoDB, Firebase, Django, Flask, etc. Use of AI tools is allowed, but the team must understand and explain their own project properly. Plagiarism or direct copying of an existing website/template will lead to disqualification. The final submission must be functional enough to demonstrate the main features. Judges&rsquo; decision will be final and binding. The entire event will be conducted in online mode. All rounds, submissions, evaluations, and presentations (if applicable) will take place virtually. Problem Statement: The problem statement will be provided only at the commencement of the event.' WHERE link = 'https://unstop.com/hackathons/webforge-a-smart-campus-webathon-manipal-university-mu-jaipur-1696902';
UPDATE public.events SET description = 'About Confluence 2.0: Confluence 2.0 is the flagship international online innovation hackathon organized by THE HELPER, bringing together student innovators, developers, designers, entrepreneurs, and problem-solvers from across the country to build impactful solutions for real-world challenges. Following the success of Confluence 1.0, which empowered hundreds of students to collaborate, innovate, and transform ideas into reality, Confluence 2.0 aims to create an even larger platform for innovation, creativity, and technological excellence. Whether you''re an experienced hacker, a first-time builder, a designer, a visionary entrepreneur, or simply someone passionate about solving meaningful problems, Confluence 2.0 is your opportunity to build, learn, collaborate, and create impact. Tracks : Participants may choose to build solutions in one or more of the following domains: Artificial Intelligence &amp; Generative AI Healthcare &amp; Well-being Education &amp; Learning Sustainability &amp; Climate Action FinTech &amp; Financial Inclusion Smart Cities &amp; Urban Innovation Accessibility &amp; Inclusive Technology Open Innovation Competition Format: Fully Online Round 1: Registration &amp; Team Formation Participants must register through the official platform. Teams may consist of: Minimum: 1 participant Maximum: 4 participants Participants may participate individually or form teams. Round 2: Idea Submission Registered teams must submit a brief overview of their idea, including: Problem Statement Proposed Solution Expected Impact Team Details Submissions will be evaluated based on innovation, relevance, feasibility, and potential impact. Round 3: PPT Shortlisting Round Shortlisted teams will be required to submit a presentation deck covering: Problem Statement Solution Overview Technical Approach Architecture / Workflow Impact &amp; Scalability Future Scope Teams will be evaluated on creativity, clarity, innovation, feasibility, and presentation quality. Round 4: Hackathon Phase Selected teams will participate in the official hackathon phase and build a working solution within the specified hackathon duration. Teams are encouraged to: Identify real-world challenges Build innovative solutions Demonstrate technical feasibility Create user-centric experiences Present measurable impact Mentorship sessions and expert guidance may be provided during this phase Round 5 : Evaluation, Judging &amp; Grand Finale Projects will be evaluated by industry professionals, mentors, and experts based on predefined judging criteria. Top-performing teams will present their solutions before the judging panel through a live demonstration and pitch session. Projects will be judged on: Innovation &amp; Creativity Technical Excellence Problem Solving Impact &amp; Scalability User Experience Presentation &amp; Demonstration Mentorship sessions and expert guidance may be provided during this phase. Eligibility : Open to students from all colleges and universities. Students from any academic discipline are eligible. Inter-college teams are allowed. Inter-specialization teams are allowed. Participants must possess a valid student ID. Individual participation is permitted. Judging Criteria: Projects will be evaluated on: Innovation &amp; Creativity Technical Implementation Problem Relevance User Experience &amp; Design Scalability Impact &amp; Feasibility Presentation &amp; Demonstration Rules &amp; Guidelines: All submitted work must be original. Teams may use open-source tools, frameworks, and APIs. Plagiarism or copying existing solutions may lead to immediate disqualification. Participants must comply with all event timelines and submission deadlines. Organizers reserve the right to disqualify any team violating event policies. Decisions made by judges and organizers will be final and binding. Teams are responsible for ensuring that submitted projects are functional and accessible during evaluation. Any form of misconduct, abuse, or unfair practice may result in disqualification. Submission Requirements: Each team may be required to submit: Project Title Problem Statement Solution Description Presentation Deck Demo Video Source Code Repository Live Prototype (if available) Why Participate? Build impactful solutions Network with innovators from across the country Learn from mentors and industry experts Showcase your skills Compete for exciting rewards and recognition Become part of the growing Confluence innovation community Confluence 2.0: Beyond the Edge of Possibility A Flagship Initiative by THE HELPER' WHERE link = 'https://unstop.com/hackathons/confluence-20-beyond-the-edge-of-possibility-srm-insitute-of-science-and-technology-1696130';
UPDATE public.events SET description = 'IdeaPulley Bug Hunt 2026 is a competitive bug-finding challenge open to testers and developers of all skill levels. Participants will explore the ideapulley.com platform and submit well-documented bug reports covering anything from critical security flaws to UI glitches and edge cases. All valid submissions will be reviewed and scored by the IdeaPulley team based on three criteria: severity of the bug, clarity of the report, and reproducibility. The higher the impact, the higher the score. Check the bugs now on www.ideapulley.com and win from perks worth $420 that is ₹40,000, that''s the prize pool so join now!!' WHERE link = 'https://unstop.com/hackathons/ideapulley-bug-hunt-2026-find-bugs-win-perks-ideapulley-1696090';
UPDATE public.events SET description = 'Welocme to Frontend Battle 3.0, 2026 , the flagship event of Web and Design Society, IIT Bhubaneswar. This isn''t your typical UI hackathon. You''ll build, optimize, and ship under real-world pressure as each stage pushes your frontend skills in a completely different direction. Expect ambitious requirements, tough constraints, and challenges that test both speed and engineering excellence. No spoilers. Just the clock, the challenge, and your chance to stand out Starts On: 26th June 2026, Ends On: 28th June 2026, Mode: &nbsp;Online (WhatsApp Group) After Registration, Join Our WhatsApp Group Number of Rounds: &nbsp;2 Eligibility Criteria: &nbsp;This challenge is open to anyone interested in the field of frontend, regardless of experience level or institution. Whether you are a seasoned developer or just starting your journey, we the team of WebnD, IIT Bhubaneswar, welcome you to the epic Frontend Battle where &ldquo;One battle rules them all&rdquo;. Also needless to say, the event being a vibe coded one, use of all the AI tools are permitted without any limitation. Frameworks Allowed: React, Next.js, Vue, Nuxt, SolidJS, Angular, or Vanilla JS. 3D frameworks like three.js are also allowed. Styling Tools : Utility CSS frameworks like Tailwind CSS, Bootstrap, or custom CSS are fully permitted. Round 1: The Qualifying Round Date: 26th June 2026 Time: The problem statement releases at 26th June 2026, 2:00 PM Duration: 4 hours Submission Deadline: 26th June 2026, 6:00 PM Description- The participants will be provided with a&nbsp; a pre-packed asset ZIP and thier goal is to build a fully responsive, SEO-optimized Web pages. Judgin Criteria and marks distribution upon features added will be mentioned in Problem Statement. Top performers advance to the finale. Round 2: The Finale Date: 28th June 2026 Time: The problem statement releases at 28th June 2026 at 10:00 AM Duration: 12 hours Submission Deadline: 28th June 2026, 10:00 PM Description: The details of this round will be revealed only to the participants who have qualified for this round Bonus : The Bounty Segment This a suprise segment to be introduced in the finale to further spice up the time bound event. Further details to be accordingly shared.' WHERE link = 'https://unstop.com/hackathons/frontend-battle-30-vibecoding-competition-indian-institute-of-technology-bhubaneswar-1696294';
